1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
"The Last Oat"

2
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:04,100
(Episode 2: Survival
Rules for the Apocalypse)

3
00:01:27,375 --> 00:01:28,375
You.

4
00:01:30,416 --> 00:01:31,957
Who are you?

5
00:01:31,958 --> 00:01:32,958
What did you do to me?

6
00:01:44,916 --> 00:01:46,196
I'm the one who saved your life.

7
00:01:49,708 --> 00:01:51,333
You'd be dead if it weren't for me.

8
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:07,291
I bandaged all your wounds.

9
00:02:08,875 --> 00:02:11,075
If I wanted to hurt you,
would I have waited this long?

10
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,166
Who asked you to save me?

11
00:02:14,416 --> 00:02:16,541
What's your real motive for saving me?

12
00:02:18,375 --> 00:02:19,735
What motive could I possibly have?

13
00:02:20,333 --> 00:02:22,290
Even if it were just an
injured stray cat or dog,

14
00:02:22,291 --> 00:02:23,750
I'd save it if I could.

15
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:25,930
Let alone a living, breathing human being.

16
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,583
Don't even think about getting
any information out of me.

17
00:02:42,166 --> 00:02:44,083
I'll just assume you
hit your head too hard.

18
00:02:44,416 --> 00:02:45,583
I won't hold it against you.

19
00:03:00,416 --> 00:03:02,332
Since I've already brought you back,

20
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:03,958
I'll take full responsibility for you.

21
00:03:04,625 --> 00:03:05,625
Relax.

22
00:03:05,833 --> 00:03:07,333
This is my secret base.

23
00:03:07,916 --> 00:03:09,583
No one else will come here.

24
00:03:16,125 --> 00:03:17,583
It's easy to die in the apocalypse.

25
00:03:18,708 --> 00:03:20,250
If you really have a death wish,

26
00:03:23,583 --> 00:03:25,875
then how did you get all those wounds?

27
00:04:06,625 --> 00:04:07,833
We're running out of food.

28
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:10,791
Shouldn't you guys discuss it
over the next couple of days?

29
00:04:11,208 --> 00:04:12,458
It's time to head out.

30
00:04:13,291 --> 00:04:14,416
Now that we have new gear,

31
00:04:14,875 --> 00:04:16,040
maybe we can go a bit further.

32
00:04:16,041 --> 00:04:17,081
And score some good stuff.

33
00:04:17,166 --> 00:04:18,166
Yeah.

34
00:04:18,541 --> 00:04:20,874
This hunting bow packs a real punch.

35
00:04:20,875 --> 00:04:23,500
It'd be great if we could each have one.

36
00:04:25,016 --> 00:04:25,516
Alright.

37
00:04:25,751 --> 00:04:27,271
I'll look into it when the time comes.

38
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:32,750
Perfect timing.

39
00:04:33,708 --> 00:04:34,999
Before we head out,

40
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,207
I'm going to reinforce the traps.

41
00:04:36,208 --> 00:04:38,488
And forage some wild berries
to stock up for Grandma Qiu.

42
00:04:53,875 --> 00:04:55,166
I won't be back for lunch.

43
00:04:55,333 --> 00:04:56,333
I brought some rations.

44
00:04:57,174 --> 00:04:57,715
Okay.

45
00:04:57,917 --> 00:05:00,290
Then Li Ming and I will hurry
up and make a plan for the trip.

46
00:05:00,291 --> 00:05:01,833
We leave in three days.

47
00:05:02,166 --> 00:05:02,666
Got it.

48
00:05:02,958 --> 00:05:04,416
Stay safe out there.

49
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,166
It's not poison.

50
00:05:47,666 --> 00:05:48,375
See for yourself.

51
00:05:48,583 --> 00:05:50,103
It's legit anti-inflammatory medicine.

52
00:06:00,916 --> 00:06:01,916
Alright then.

53
00:06:03,541 --> 00:06:06,625
Let me check your wounds
and change your bandages first.

54
00:06:27,083 --> 00:06:29,291
How did you get all these injuries?

55
00:06:30,708 --> 00:06:32,188
Why were you passed out in the woods?

56
00:06:32,958 --> 00:06:34,767
I was passing through
while scavenging for supplies.

57
00:06:34,791 --> 00:06:35,911
Ran into a horde of zombies.

58
00:06:36,791 --> 00:06:38,708
Didn't expect there to be a camp nearby.

59
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,458
Then you're pretty lucky.

60
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:43,750
You ran into me.

61
00:06:46,916 --> 00:06:47,916
Barely.

62
00:06:54,291 --> 00:06:55,457
This camp...

63
00:06:55,458 --> 00:06:58,791
How long has this place you picked been here?

64
00:07:00,625 --> 00:07:03,305
We all spent a long time
searching for before settling down.

65
00:07:04,625 --> 00:07:06,505
This area is easy to
defend and hard to attack.

66
00:07:08,625 --> 00:07:09,708
Your companions

67
00:07:10,416 --> 00:07:11,416
are pretty impressive.

68
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,583
Everyone will definitely
give it their all to survive.

69
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,874
I've also researched a
lot of defensive measures.

70
00:07:28,875 --> 00:07:30,635
We even intercepted
three zombies yesterday.

71
00:07:35,541 --> 00:07:38,000
You're pretty desperate to survive too.

72
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:39,708
You must really want to live.

73
00:07:41,833 --> 00:07:43,673
Then why didn't you ask
me for help back then?

74
00:07:44,125 --> 00:07:45,245
Instead, you chased me away.

75
00:07:47,708 --> 00:07:49,668
Who knew if you were
going to hurt me or save me?

76
00:07:55,625 --> 00:07:58,625
Now you know I'm not a bad person, right?

77
00:08:05,958 --> 00:08:06,958
Don't move.

78
00:09:08,541 --> 00:09:10,166
The wound is still a bit inflamed.

79
00:09:11,041 --> 00:09:13,121
You need to take
anti-inflammatories to heal faster.

80
00:09:30,541 --> 00:09:31,375
That's more like it.

81
00:09:31,541 --> 00:09:33,000
Why make things hard on yourself?

82
00:09:35,291 --> 00:09:36,291
Let go!

83
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:38,333
Let go!

84
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,083
What are you doing?

85
00:09:42,958 --> 00:09:44,624
If you want to survive in the apocalypse,

86
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:46,905
zombies aren't the only things
you need to guard against.

87
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:52,291
I can tell who's good and who's bad.

88
00:09:52,875 --> 00:09:54,416
I know you're not a bad person.

89
00:09:58,125 --> 00:09:59,458
But you're not a good one either.

90
00:10:11,708 --> 00:10:12,708
No dinner for you today.

91
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,041
Get some rest and heal up.

92
00:10:22,083 --> 00:10:23,083
What a jerk.

93
00:10:35,750 --> 00:10:37,250
All bark and no bite.

94
00:12:26,541 --> 00:12:28,791
This time we're heading
to the school out east.

95
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:29,916
Lin Zai,

96
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,375
are you sure there
are still supplies there?

97
00:12:32,708 --> 00:12:33,708
Yeah.

98
00:12:33,916 --> 00:12:37,041
It's just that we were
attacked by zombies back then.

99
00:12:38,666 --> 00:12:40,833
We've already picked the
surrounding areas clean.

100
00:12:41,041 --> 00:12:42,625
We have to take a risk this time.

101
00:12:44,916 --> 00:12:45,916
Alright.

102
00:12:46,833 --> 00:12:48,273
I remember the layout of the school.

103
00:12:48,583 --> 00:12:50,184
But we still need to be extremely careful.

104
00:12:50,208 --> 00:12:52,041
I've got all the gear we need ready.

105
00:12:53,958 --> 00:12:54,958
The traps around the camp

106
00:12:54,959 --> 00:12:56,415
have all been reinforced and checked.

107
00:12:56,416 --> 00:12:57,833
They'll keep Grandma Qiu safe.

108
00:12:58,041 --> 00:12:59,625
Alright, let's head out immediately.

109
00:12:59,708 --> 00:13:01,875
If anything goes wrong,
we pull back at once.

110
00:13:02,583 --> 00:13:03,583
Got it.

111
00:13:10,875 --> 00:13:12,250
Are there zombies?

112
00:14:06,666 --> 00:14:07,750
You're not dead.

113
00:14:08,833 --> 00:14:10,333
I'm here to get my stuff back.

114
00:14:11,125 --> 00:14:12,125
Sorry,

115
00:14:12,375 --> 00:14:14,750
finders keepers.

116
00:14:23,541 --> 00:14:24,541
Stay back!

117
00:14:27,375 --> 00:14:28,208
Don't move!

118
00:14:28,208 --> 00:14:29,208
Don't come any closer!

119
00:14:50,541 --> 00:14:53,583
Give me my backpack
back, exactly as it was.

120
00:14:55,583 --> 00:14:57,458
I know you won't hurt me.

121
00:14:58,541 --> 00:15:00,250
I won't hurt any of you.

122
00:15:01,250 --> 00:15:02,958
As long as you return what's mine.

123
00:15:04,250 --> 00:15:06,000
But if you insist on keeping it,

124
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:08,708
you're forcing my hand.

125
00:15:22,791 --> 00:15:23,875
Give it all back to him.

126
00:15:26,750 --> 00:15:27,791
What is this junk?

127
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,583
The watch on your wrist is mine too.

128
00:15:51,041 --> 00:15:51,791
It was my idea

129
00:15:51,791 --> 00:15:52,791
to take your things.

130
00:15:53,250 --> 00:15:54,625
But I also saved your life.

131
00:15:56,958 --> 00:15:57,958
Let's call it even.

132
00:15:58,125 --> 00:15:59,125
Just go.

133
00:16:18,291 --> 00:16:19,125
Guangqi.

134
00:16:19,125 --> 00:16:20,125
Calling HQ.

135
00:16:20,875 --> 00:16:21,875
Signal lost.

136
00:16:21,958 --> 00:16:23,558
Unable to establish a stable connection.

137
00:16:24,666 --> 00:16:26,826
Checking the operational
status of other core modules.

138
00:16:26,958 --> 00:16:27,958
Network unavailable.

139
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,480
Positioning module accuracy degraded.

140
00:16:31,791 --> 00:16:32,915
Physiological module detects

141
00:16:32,916 --> 00:16:34,207
surface trauma on the user

142
00:16:34,208 --> 00:16:35,375
and signs of mild infection.

143
00:16:35,791 --> 00:16:37,458
Sample escort protocol updated.

144
00:16:37,583 --> 00:16:39,041
Immune target confirmed.

145
00:19:01,958 --> 00:19:02,625
Sister Chen,

146
00:19:02,958 --> 00:19:03,958
Brother Li,

147
00:19:04,458 --> 00:19:05,458
I'm sorry.

148
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:08,660
I shouldn't have lied to you.

149
00:19:09,375 --> 00:19:11,250
But I really didn't know he'd attack us.

150
00:19:11,583 --> 00:19:12,749
It's all my fault.

151
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:14,083
Just beat me up.

152
00:19:27,375 --> 00:19:28,655
Let's forget about it this time.

153
00:19:28,875 --> 00:19:30,249
We checked that day,

154
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:32,090
and that guy really
wasn't bitten by a zombie.

155
00:19:32,375 --> 00:19:33,791
But we still left him to die.

156
00:19:35,208 --> 00:19:37,458
We really didn't need to be so ruthless.

157
00:19:37,708 --> 00:19:39,908
We could have at least left
him some food and medicine.

158
00:19:40,166 --> 00:19:41,875
Lin Zai, you did the right thing.

159
00:19:42,791 --> 00:19:44,958
This incident serves
as a wake-up call for us.

160
00:19:45,708 --> 00:19:46,958
We fight to survive,

161
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:48,625
not just for ourselves,

162
00:19:49,375 --> 00:19:51,333
but for all of humanity.

163
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,833
If you insist on apologizing,

164
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:58,500
carry more supplies.

165
00:20:03,958 --> 00:20:06,000
What are you looking at me for?

166
00:20:06,041 --> 00:20:08,375
I'm not helping you this time.

167
00:20:09,833 --> 00:20:10,666
No need.

168
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:13,040
Brother Li, I just saw a few
bottles of that liquor you like.

169
00:20:13,041 --> 00:20:13,750
I'll grab a few for you

170
00:20:13,750 --> 00:20:14,750
as an apology.

171
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,165
Sounds good.

172
00:20:16,166 --> 00:20:17,457
But you can only bring two bottles at most.

173
00:20:17,458 --> 00:20:18,665
Prioritize essential supplies.

174
00:20:18,666 --> 00:20:19,666
I know.

175
00:20:21,833 --> 00:20:22,875
Minding other people's business, huh.

176
00:20:39,375 --> 00:20:40,375
Run!

177
00:20:43,041 --> 00:20:44,041
Get out of here!
